# Cross-domain imports

A domain is a folder under `$lib/` (or `$shared/repositories`, `$shared/providers`) with its own layers.
When one domain needs another, it imports the other domain's api file, never a path inside it.

## Renderer side

A renderer file (`domain/`, `application/`, `infrastructure/`, `presentation/`, an api file, a flat `$shared/<util>`) may import:

- its own domain, following the layer rules;
- `$lib/<domain>/<domain>.api.ts`;
- `$shared/repositories/repositories.api.ts` and `$shared/providers/providers.api.ts`;
- flat `$shared/<util>/**` modules (`router`, `extensions`, `errors`, `storage`, ...);
- `$contract`, `$hyper-ui`, and packages.

A `domain/` file is narrower and wider at once: it may import another domain's `domain/` folder, and nothing but `domain/` folders, `$contract` and `ts-pattern` (see `layers/domain-layer.mdc`).

Anything else inside another domain is `crossDomainDeepImport`.
A relative path that leaves the domain folder is `escapesDomain`.

## What an api file may export

- A domain api exports from its own presentation layer only.
- A shared domain api (`repositories.api.ts`, `providers.api.ts`) may also export its domain types, pure functions, queries, commands and hooks.
- Infrastructure and platform never cross an api file, anywhere.
  The check is `apiExportsInternals`.
- If a symbol is missing from an api, move it to a shared domain.
  Do not widen the api.

## The `app` consumer domain

`$lib/app` owns the shell, the sidebar, the layouts, the pages and the routes.
It may additionally import `$lib/<domain>/application/**` of any domain, so a page can call a command and read a query without a render prop.
It still may not reach another domain's `infrastructure/`, `presentation/` internals, `domain/` internals or `platform/`.
No domain imports `app`.

## Main-process side

A `platform/` folder or a `<domain>.platform.ts` file may import:

- its own domain;
- another domain's `<domain>.platform.ts` (for example `$shared/repositories/repositories.platform.ts`);
- `$main/**`, `$contract`, `node:*`, `electron`, and packages.

It never imports a renderer layer, an api file, a flat `$shared/<util>`, or `$hyper-ui` (`platformImportsRenderer`).
It never imports another domain's `domain/` or `platform/` internals (`crossDomainDeepImport`).
A renderer file never imports platform code or `$main` (`rendererImportsPlatform`).

`src/main/modules.ts` and `src/main/index.ts` are composition roots: they may import any `platform/` file, in practice each domain's `platform/register.ts`.
Other `src/main` files may import any domain's `domain/` folder and `<domain>.platform.ts`.

## Everywhere

No `index.ts` and no `export *` (`barrelFile`, `starExport`).
No relative path that leaves the domain folder (`escapesDomain`).
